WEBVTT

NOTE Captions are the agent's own words, taken from its trace.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.720
<c.run>List session directory contents</c>

2
00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:17.820
<c.run>Read tool headers and robot status</c>

3
00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:22.900
<c.run>Extract cropped demo frames at 1fps</c>

4
00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:31.740
<c.run>Extract demo frames and build contact sheets</c>

5
00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:51.740
<c.run>Get robot state and capture frames</c>

6
00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:44.510
<c.run>Crop zoomed views of parts</c>

7
00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:21.100
<c.run>Deproject top-image part locations</c>

8
00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:31.480
<c.run>Read rest of geo/facefit and compute view pose</c>

9
00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:35.740
<c.run>Compute wrist viewing pose over parts</c>

10
00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:55.740
<c.run>Move to overview pose and capture</c>

11
00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:18.520
<c.run>Deproject wrist pixels using depth</c>

12
00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:19.745
<c.think>The bolt and big cylinder are standing upright while the
nut and ring lie flat, so I need to drop the nut over
the bolt shaft and the ring over the cylinder.</c>

13
00:03:19.745 --> 00:03:20.450
<c.think>I'll grab close-up views next to nail down the exact
geometry.</c>

14
00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:37.980
<c.run>Move closer over nut and bolt, capture wrist</c>

15
00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:57.980
<c.run>Check HSV and fit nut top face</c>

16
00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:23.040
<c.run>Fit nut outline on its top plane</c>

17
00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:36.250
<c.run>View bolt top close-up</c>

18
00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:39.670
<c.run>Get bolt top height and HSV samples</c>

19
00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:59.670
<c.run>Fit bolt shaft top rim</c>

20
00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:22.120
<c.run>Measure bolt head height from depth</c>

21
00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:41.010
<c.run>Move above nut and capture</c>

22
00:05:41.010 --> 00:05:45.430
<c.run>Check nut alignment with grasp point</c>

23
00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:56.250
<c.run>Descend to nut grasp height</c>

24
00:05:56.250 --> 00:06:02.630
<c.run>Close gripper on nut</c>

25
00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:17.540
<c.run>Lift nut and capture</c>

26
00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:35.720
<c.run>Measure nut offset in hand</c>

27
00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:44.470
<c.run>Locate held nut's far vertex</c>

28
00:06:44.470 --> 00:07:03.350
<c.run>Sample depth points on held nut</c>

29
00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:09.140
<c.run>Fit held nut hole edge circle</c>

30
00:07:09.140 --> 00:07:29.140
<c.run>Zoom nut crop and sample HSV</c>

31
00:07:45.200 --> 00:08:05.200
<c.run>Fit visible hole rim arc of held nut</c>

32
00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:20.790
<c.run>Move nut above bolt shaft and capture</c>

33
00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:30.910
<c.run>Crop top view around bolt</c>

34
00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:42.810
<c.run>Project shaft and hole centers into wrist image</c>

35
00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:52.040
<c.run>Lower nut onto shaft top</c>

36
00:08:52.040 --> 00:09:04.590
<c.run>Lower nut further along shaft</c>

37
00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:11.110
<c.run>Lower nut closer to bolt head</c>

38
00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:22.410
<c.run>Release nut and capture</c>

39
00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:41.000
<c.run>Lift and view the bolt-nut assembly</c>

40
00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:51.280
<c.run>Check nut resting height via depth</c>

41
00:09:51.280 --> 00:10:11.280
<c.run>Move to view the tall cylinder</c>

42
00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:26.800
<c.run>Measure cylinder top and fit rim</c>

43
00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:33.280
<c.run>Sample HSV and fit cylinder top rim</c>

44
00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:41.190
<c.run>Refit cylinder rim with lower V floor</c>

45
00:10:41.190 --> 00:10:58.420
<c.run>View ring close-up</c>

46
00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:06.330
<c.run>Measure ring height and colours</c>

47
00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:21.610
<c.run>Fit ring outline at its top plane</c>

48
00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:29.790
<c.run>Move above ring and capture</c>

49
00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:33.170
<c.run>Refit ring from closer view</c>

50
00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:43.070
<c.run>Descend around ring</c>

51
00:11:43.070 --> 00:11:48.770
<c.run>Close gripper on ring</c>

52
00:11:48.770 --> 00:12:08.770
<c.run>Lift ring and capture</c>

53
00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:33.830
<c.run>Measure held ring offset from image</c>

54
00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:53.510
<c.run>Move ring above cylinder</c>

55
00:12:53.510 --> 00:13:03.850
<c.run>Lower ring onto cylinder top</c>

56
00:13:03.850 --> 00:13:14.460
<c.run>Lower ring along cylinder</c>

57
00:13:14.460 --> 00:13:23.910
<c.run>Release ring and capture</c>

58
00:13:23.910 --> 00:13:41.100
<c.run>Lift and view ring-cylinder assembly</c>

59
00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:47.460
<c.run>Check ring resting height via depth</c>

60
00:13:47.460 --> 00:13:54.270
<c.run>Crop top view of assemblies</c>

61
00:13:54.270 --> 00:14:08.730
<c.run>Lift, return home, capture final frames</c>

62
00:14:08.730 --> 00:14:18.740
<c.run>Crop final top view</c>

63
00:14:18.740 --> 00:14:38.740
<c.think>Both assemblies now match the goal image, and the arm is
back in the observe posture with the gripper open. I'll
check the state and write the result.</c>

64
00:14:50.320 --> 00:15:00.760
<c.run>Write kept tool with header and verify it runs</c>

65
00:15:00.760 --> 00:15:18.467
<c.say>I think this one worked: the robot put both blue parts
on their matching white parts.</c>
